WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.798
Hi, friends. This is the Letting-Go Leaf.

00:00:12.798 --> 00:00:17.597
Sit tall in your chair. Feet flat on the floor.

00:00:17.597 --> 00:00:20.476
Hands flat on your desk. Shoulders soft.

00:00:20.476 --> 00:00:23.355
Take one slow breath with me… and let it go.

00:00:23.355 --> 00:00:34.872
Thoughts and feelings come and go, all day long — like leaves floating on a slow, quiet stream.

00:00:34.872 --> 00:00:43.509
Some thoughts float by quickly. Some get stuck, and go around and around in your head.

00:00:43.509 --> 00:00:49.267
The Letting-Go Leaf teaches us to notice a stuck thought — and let it float by.

00:00:49.267 --> 00:00:58.864
Picture a slow stream. The water is calm. Green leaves float on top, one by one.

00:00:58.864 --> 00:01:09.421
Here comes a leaf with a happy thought: "I like this day." Notice it… and let it float by.

00:01:09.421 --> 00:01:17.098
Here comes another leaf. This one carries a stuck thought: "I can't do this."

00:01:17.098 --> 00:01:23.816
Notice it, and say quietly to yourself: "There is the I-can't thought."

00:01:23.816 --> 00:01:31.494
Now watch it float. The water carries it slowly… past you… and away.

00:01:31.494 --> 00:01:41.091
You do not have to hold the thought. You do not have to push it away. Just let it float.

00:01:41.091 --> 00:01:46.849
Here comes one more leaf, with a worried thought: "What if I get it wrong?" Notice it… and let it float by, too.

00:01:46.849 --> 00:01:57.406
If a thought comes back on another leaf, that is okay. Thoughts do that. Notice it again, and let it float by again. The stream keeps moving.

00:01:57.406 --> 00:02:03.164
You are standing on the bank, watching the leaves. The thoughts float by — and you stay here, calm and steady.

00:02:03.164 --> 00:02:07.003
Hands down. One more slow breath… and let it go.

00:02:07.003 --> 00:02:08.922
Eyes open. Look around your classroom.

00:02:08.922 --> 00:02:12.761
You're ready for what's next.
